      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You can use the system culture info to get a two or three letter string of the current system language:\n\nSystem Language: System.Globalization.CultureInfo.CurrentCulture\n\nUI Language: System.Globalization.CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture\n\nFrom these you can get the TwoLetterISOLanguageName or ThreeLetterISOLanguageName.\n\nEnglish - \"en\" \"eng\"\n\nJapanese - \"ja\" \"jpn\"\n\nGermen - \"de\" \"deu\"\n\nChinese - \"zh\" \"zho\"\n\netc.\n\nSee more here:\n\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.globalization.cultureinfo.threeletterisolanguagename?view=net-8.0",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
