  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-02-17T19:22:45.510Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "We currently have methods to get both the selected VRChat UI Language VRCPlayerApi.GetCurrentLanguage()\n\nas well as supported UI Languages VRCPlayerAPI.GetAvailableLanguages()\n\nHowever it is possible the system language may not match these, or be a unsupported language.\n\nI would like the ability to get the system language to be able to supply in world translations when the system language falls out of these ranges.\n\nEG, in LS Media we currently get the current vrchat language to automatically select subtitle language without manual interaction, However youtube supports many more languages than VRChat does.\n\nHaving access to this would allow us to support any language subtitle automatically, providing a better user experience in general.\n\nClientsim also returns incorrect information for these methods currently,\n\nSee https://github.com/vrchat-community/ClientSim/pull/111",
